On Jul 11, 2:06 am, "Joseph N. Hall" <remid0d...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Hi. I'm wondering, what relatively simple evolutionary tweaks and
> features would you like to see added to NetHack?

- Magic resistance should be made less essential.  (Maybe by
introducing a minor version of it that does its most important things
and is more common/easier to have.  True magic resistance would have
to be made rarer then, however.  I still think my old idea for a Ring
vs. Death Magic is valid.)
- Unicorn horns are overpowered.  I still don't see how someone can
think otherwise.
- Stat gains have become too common while the effects of stats have
become proportionally less of the game.  Stat increases (especially
from exercise and blessed potions of gain ability) should be made less
common, and their effects should be made subtly greater.
- There should be many more high-level monsters that can give a very
experienced character trouble.  Free sources of levels should be
scaled back somewhat.  (They should NOT be removed completely.  Free
level gain is part of what makes Nethack what it is.)  The player's
maximum level should be increased a bit, too.
- Monster difficulty should be more decoupled from player level.  The
very reason things like the protection racket and Dive For Victory can
work is that players know they'll face weaker opponents than they
would be otherwise.
- Look at the patch database for the most interesting game additions.
There's some good ideas in Biodiversity, the level flipping patch, the
patches that add more versions of the major non-random levels, Color
Alchemy, and so on.
- More branches!  More items!  More treasure!  More spells!  More,
more, MOAR!

